      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "9.1 Scheduled Tribes (STs) of Andhra Pradesh"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "Andhra Pradesh hosts 7 Particularly Vulnerable Tribal Groups (PVTGs) including the Chenchu, Konda Reddi, and Kolam.",
        "Sugalis (Lambadas) form the largest tribal community in terms of overall population within the state.",
        "Tribal movements in AP, notably the Rampa Rebellion led by Alluri Sitarama Raju, fought fiercely against British colonial forest restrictions.",
        "Scheduled Areas in Andhra Pradesh are governed under the Fifth Schedule of the Indian Constitution, providing legislative protections like Act 1/70."
      ],
      "id": "94zvn4v"
    },
